{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_38","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -c 'select(.claim_id >= \\\"ABS-0061\\\" and .claim_id <= \\\"ABS-0108\\\") | {claim_id,claim_text,subject,search_terms_suggested}' _run/s9/p4/absence-claims.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"{\"claim_id\":\"ABS-0061\",\"claim_text\":\"the court did not reach whether Kopchak's cupping his hands against the window was itself an unlawful trespass\",\"subject\":\"Whether cupping hands against a car window is an unlawful trespass\",\"search_terms_suggested\":[\"Loines cupping hands window trespass not reached\",\"plain view window trespass alternative ground\"]}\n{\"claim_id\":\"ABS-0062\",\"claim_text\":\"no Supreme Court or Fourth Circuit case had ever extended the collective-knowledge doctrine beyond the context of information or instructions communicated\",\"subject\":\"Horizontal aggregation under the collective-knowledge doctrine\",\"search_terms_suggested\":[\"collective knowledge horizontal aggregation\",\"Massenburg no case expanded collective knowledge\"]}\n{\"claim_id\":\"ABS-0063\",\"claim_text\":\"The court therefore did not reach the independent-source or good-faith questions\",\"subject\":\"Independent-source and good-faith questions (not reached)\",\"search_terms_suggested\":[\"May-Shaw independent source good faith not reached\",\"pole camera curtilage alternative grounds\"]}\n{\"claim_id\":\"ABS-0064\",\"claim_text\":\"the court did not need to resolve whether the more intrusive **forensic** DOMEX extraction required reasonable suspicion\",\"subject\":\"Whether a forensic border device extraction requires reasonable suspicion\",\"search_terms_suggested\":[\"forensic DOMEX extraction reasonable suspicion\",\"Mendez did not resolve forensic border search\"]}\n{\"claim_id\":\"ABS-0065\",\"claim_text\":\"it **leaves open** the forensic-search standard\",\"subject\":\"Forensic border device search standard (live circuit split)\",\"search_terms_suggested\":[\"forensic border device search standard split\",\"Mendez leaves open forensic standard Kolsuz Cano Touset\"]}\n{\"claim_id\":\"ABS-0066\",\"claim_text\":\"the decision established no binding circuit rule on whether such surveillance is a search\",\"subject\":\"Whether prolonged pole-camera surveillance of a home is a search (no binding 1st Cir rule)\",\"search_terms_suggested\":[\"pole camera surveillance search no binding circuit rule\",\"Moore-Bush en banc 3-3 no rule\"]}\n{\"claim_id\":\"ABS-0067\",\"claim_text\":\"its opinions establish no binding circuit rule on that question\",\"subject\":\"No binding First Circuit rule on pole-camera-as-search\",\"search_terms_suggested\":[\"Moore-Bush no binding circuit rule pole camera\",\"First Circuit pole camera search no rule\"]}\n{\"claim_id\":\"ABS-0068\",\"claim_text\":\"the surveillance-is-a-search question remains unresolved in the First Circuit\",\"subject\":\"Pole-camera-as-search question unresolved in the First Circuit\",\"search_terms_suggested\":[\"pole camera search unresolved First Circuit\",\"Moore-Bush open question surveillance search\"]}\n{\"claim_id\":\"ABS-0069\",\"claim_text\":\"expressly declined to reach the underlying Fourth Amendment question\",\"subject\":\"Underlying Fourth Amendment question on phone-search warrant scope\",\"search_terms_suggested\":[\"Morton declined to reach Fourth Amendment phone warrant\",\"en banc good faith declined merits phone search\"]}\n{\"claim_id\":\"ABS-0070\",\"claim_text\":\"the unresolved digital-search problem the majority left open\",\"subject\":\"Whether the plain-view doctrine needs a digital-search exception\",\"search_terms_suggested\":[\"plain view digital exception unresolved\",\"Morton concurrence plain view data warrant scope\"]}\n{\"claim_id\":\"ABS-0071\",\"claim_text\":\"it expressly declined to decide whether the warrants were overbroad as to the phones' photographs\",\"subject\":\"Whether the phone-photo warrants were overbroad\",\"search_terms_suggested\":[\"Morton overbroad phone photo warrant declined\",\"particularity phone photographs not decided\"]}\n{\"claim_id\":\"ABS-0072\",\"claim_text\":\"the panel therefore did not reach the government's alternative *Maldonaldo-Espinosa* ground\",\"subject\":\"Alternative Maldonaldo-Espinosa ground (not reached)\",\"search_terms_suggested\":[\"Perez alternative ground not reached search incident\",\"backpack search incident alternative ground\"]}\n{\"claim_id\":\"ABS-0073\",\"claim_text\":\"Note the live cross-circuit tension over how far the doctrine reaches when no human at the private company ever viewed the specific file — the Ninth Circuit has diverged on that point\",\"subject\":\"Hash-match private-search doctrine cross-circuit tension\",\"search_terms_suggested\":[\"hash match private search circuit split\",\"Reddick Ninth Circuit diverged hash match\"]}\n{\"claim_id\":\"ABS-0074\",\"claim_text\":\"That reading divides the courts\",\"subject\":\"Split on frisking an armed-but-not-shown-dangerous stopped person\",\"search_terms_suggested\":[\"armed dangerous frisk Terry split\",\"Robinson 4th Cir en banc open carry frisk split\"]}\n{\"claim_id\":\"ABS-0075\",\"claim_text\":\"The Court left open, without applying, a separate due-process limit for the most extreme cases\",\"subject\":\"Outrageous-government-conduct due-process limit\",\"search_terms_suggested\":[\"outrageous government conduct due process limit\",\"Russell left open due process defense\"]}\n{\"claim_id\":\"ABS-0076\",\"claim_text\":\"the court noted that the Tenth Circuit reached a different conclusion\",\"subject\":\"Circuit split on tent/public-land REP (Sandoval vs Ruckman)\",\"search_terms_suggested\":[\"tent public land reasonable expectation privacy split\",\"Sandoval Ruckman circuit split camping\"]}\n{\"claim_id\":\"ABS-0077\",\"claim_text\":\"That reading of *[[Nix v. Williams]]* divides the circuits\",\"subject\":\"Inevitable-discovery active-pursuit circuit split\",\"search_terms_suggested\":[\"inevitable discovery active pursuit split\",\"Satterfield Nix active pursuit circuits divide\"]}\n{\"claim_id\":\"ABS-0078\",\"claim_text\":\"the categorical general-warrant holding remains binding only in the Fifth Circuit\",\"subject\":\"Geofence categorical general-warrant rule binding only in the Fifth Circuit\",\"search_terms_suggested\":[\"geofence general warrant Fifth Circuit only\",\"Smith 2024 categorical general warrant minority\"]}\n{\"claim_id\":\"ABS-0079\",\"claim_text\":\"it did not decide whether any geofence warrant can satisfy probable cause and [[Particularity|particularity]], so *Smith*'s stronger point remains the minority answer to a question SCOTUS left open\",\"subject\":\"Whether any geofence warrant can satisfy probable cause and particularity\",\"search_terms_suggested\":[\"geofence warrant probable cause particularity open\",\"Smith 2024 minority answer SCOTUS left open\"]}\n{\"claim_id\":\"ABS-0080\",\"claim_text\":\"Circuit split: the 9th Cir. (United States v. Cotterman) requires reasonable suspicion for forensic device searches at the border\",\"subject\":\"Circuit split on suspicion for forensic border device searches\",\"search_terms_suggested\":[\"forensic border device search circuit split\",\"Touset Cotterman split reasonable suspicion\"]}\n{\"claim_id\":\"ABS-0081\",\"claim_text\":\"the Supreme Court has never required suspicion to search **property** (as opposed to highly intrusive searches of the **person**) at the border\",\"subject\":\"Whether the Supreme Court requires suspicion to search property at the border\",\"search_terms_suggested\":[\"Supreme Court suspicion search property border\",\"Touset no SCOTUS suspicion border property\"]}\n{\"claim_id\":\"ABS-0082\",\"claim_text\":\"a recognized split on suspicion requirements for device searches at the border\",\"subject\":\"Recognized split on suspicion for border device searches\",\"search_terms_suggested\":[\"border device search suspicion split\",\"Touset rejects Cotterman recognized split\"]}\n{\"claim_id\":\"ABS-0083\",\"claim_text\":\"Issue of first impression; courts split on long-term pole-camera surveillance\",\"subject\":\"Long-term pole-camera surveillance (first impression; courts split)\",\"search_terms_suggested\":[\"pole camera surveillance first impression split\",\"Tuggle long-term pole camera issue of first impression\"]}\n{\"claim_id\":\"ABS-0084\",\"claim_text\":\"Whether prolonged warrantless pole-camera surveillance of a home's exterior is a \\\"search\\\" was an issue of first impression in the Seventh Circuit\",\"subject\":\"Whether prolonged pole-camera surveillance is a search (first impression, 7th Cir)\",\"search_terms_suggested\":[\"prolonged pole camera search first impression Seventh Circuit\",\"Tuggle issue of first impression pole camera\"]}\n{\"claim_id\":\"ABS-0085\",\"claim_text\":\"Courts remain split on the question\",\"subject\":\"Courts split on pole-camera surveillance / Carpenter mosaic\",\"search_terms_suggested\":[\"pole camera Carpenter mosaic courts split\",\"Tuggle unresolved tension mosaic theory\"]}\n{\"claim_id\":\"ABS-0086\",\"claim_text\":\"presenting the open question of how certain officers must be before forcing entry into a dwelling to make an arrest\",\"subject\":\"How certain officers must be before forcing entry to arrest\",\"search_terms_suggested\":[\"Payton reason to believe quantum entry arrest\",\"Vasquez-Algarin open question forcing entry\"]}\n{\"claim_id\":\"ABS-0087\",\"claim_text\":\"note the acknowledged circuit split, with some courts treating \\\"reason to believe\\\" as a lesser standard than probable cause\",\"subject\":\"Circuit split on Payton 'reason to believe' quantum\",\"search_terms_suggested\":[\"Payton reason to believe probable cause split\",\"Vasquez-Algarin acknowledged circuit split\"]}\n{\"claim_id\":\"ABS-0088\",\"claim_text\":\"an unresolved split worth teaching\",\"subject\":\"Hash-match private-search doctrine split (Wilson vs Reddick/Miller)\",\"search_terms_suggested\":[\"hash match private search split circuits\",\"Wilson Ninth Circuit diverges Reddick Miller\"]}\n{\"claim_id\":\"ABS-0089\",\"claim_text\":\"but did not decide whether it is required, because CBP had reasonable suspicion\",\"subject\":\"Whether reasonable suspicion is required for a forensic border device search\",\"search_terms_suggested\":[\"Xiang forensic device search suspicion required\",\"outbound border search reasonable suspicion not decided\"]}\n{\"claim_id\":\"ABS-0090\",\"claim_text\":\"note the unresolved circuit split on the precise standard for forensic device searches\",\"subject\":\"Circuit split on the standard for forensic border device searches\",\"search_terms_suggested\":[\"forensic border device search standard split\",\"Xiang unresolved circuit split forensic\"]}\n{\"claim_id\":\"ABS-0091\",\"claim_text\":\"The Court did not decide whether Bradford, who self-censored rather than being directly enjoined, had likewise suffered a past, completed injury\",\"subject\":\"Whether a self-censoring plaintiff suffered a completed injury\",\"search_terms_suggested\":[\"Uzuegbunam Bradford completed injury not decided\",\"nominal damages self-censor standing reserved\"]}\n{\"claim_id\":\"ABS-0092\",\"claim_text\":\"the Court left open a potential alternative ground concerning what White witnessed\",\"subject\":\"Alternative qualified-immunity ground concerning what the officer witnessed\",\"search_terms_suggested\":[\"White v. Pauly alternative ground left open\",\"qualified immunity what officer witnessed\"]}\n{\"claim_id\":\"ABS-0093\",\"claim_text\":\"a deferential AEDPA holding that did not decide, on [[Common Legal Terms#de-novo|de novo]] review, whether age is categorically irrelevant\",\"subject\":\"Whether age is categorically irrelevant to Miranda custody (de novo)\",\"search_terms_suggested\":[\"juvenile age Miranda custody de novo\",\"Alvarado AEDPA did not decide age J.D.B.\"]}\n{\"claim_id\":\"ABS-0094\",\"claim_text\":\"Circuit/state authority only; no SCOTUS\",\"subject\":\"No recent SCOTUS on the voluntariness lower-court frontier\",\"search_terms_suggested\":[\"voluntariness confession no SCOTUS recent\",\"due process voluntariness circuit developments\"]}\n{\"claim_id\":\"ABS-0095\",\"claim_text\":\"the live action sits in two places: how the circuits apply *[[Missouri v. Seibert|Seibert]]*'s fractured opinion to the deliberate two-step\",\"subject\":\"Circuit application of Seibert's two-step and Shatzer's break-in-custody\",\"search_terms_suggested\":[\"Seibert two-step deliberate circuits\",\"Shatzer break in custody lower courts\"]}\n{\"claim_id\":\"ABS-0096\",\"claim_text\":\"Circuit split, with no SCOTUS case pending to resolve it\",\"subject\":\"Circuit split on Seibert's controlling rationale (no SCOTUS pending)\",\"search_terms_suggested\":[\"Seibert Marks narrowest holding split\",\"Capers Williams deliberate two-step circuit split\"]}\n{\"claim_id\":\"ABS-0097\",\"claim_text\":\"the circuits diverge on how far the public-safety exception reaches once an arrestee is secured\",\"subject\":\"Reach of the public-safety exception after a suspect is secured\",\"search_terms_suggested\":[\"public safety exception secured arrestee split\",\"Quarles scope circuits diverge secured suspect\"]}\n{\"claim_id\":\"ABS-0098\",\"claim_text\":\"the opinion expressly acknowledges a **circuit split\",\"subject\":\"Circuit split on the breadth of the public-safety exception (Liddell)\",\"search_terms_suggested\":[\"public safety exception circuit split Liddell\",\"Quarles broad reading Eighth Circuit split\"]}\n{\"claim_id\":\"ABS-0099\",\"claim_text\":\"No SCOTUS case is pending on these points\",\"subject\":\"No pending SCOTUS on Garrity self-executing/POBR frontiers\",\"search_terms_suggested\":[\"Garrity self-executing immunity no SCOTUS\",\"Kalkines warning POBR frontier no Supreme Court\"]}\n{\"claim_id\":\"ABS-0100\",\"claim_text\":\"whether the disclosure duty reaches the **pre-plea** stage, where the circuits have divided and the Supreme Court has so far declined to resolve it\",\"subject\":\"Whether the Brady disclosure duty reaches the pre-plea stage\",\"search_terms_suggested\":[\"Brady pre-plea disclosure circuits divided\",\"Supreme Court declined to resolve pre-plea Brady\"]}\n{\"claim_id\":\"ABS-0101\",\"claim_text\":\"(2019), leaving the split intact\",\"subject\":\"Pre-plea Brady split left intact by cert denial (Alvarez)\",\"search_terms_suggested\":[\"Brady pre-plea split cert denied\",\"Alvarez en banc split intact certiorari denied\"]}\n{\"claim_id\":\"ABS-0102\",\"claim_text\":\"The Court reserved the possibility that \\\"some day ... [police conduct may be] so outrageous that due process principles\",\"subject\":\"Reserved outrageous-government-conduct due-process defense\",\"search_terms_suggested\":[\"outrageous government conduct due process reserved\",\"Russell Hampton due process defense reserved dictum\"]}\n{\"claim_id\":\"ABS-0103\",\"claim_text\":\"the two-element test produces divergence on the facts, not a split on the rule\",\"subject\":\"Assertion of no circuit split on the entrapment test\",\"search_terms_suggested\":[\"entrapment two-element test no split\",\"Jacobson predisposition divergence facts not rule\"]}\n{\"claim_id\":\"ABS-0104\",\"claim_text\":\"Circuit and state developments only; no SCOTUS\",\"subject\":\"No recent SCOTUS on the eyewitness-identification frontier\",\"search_terms_suggested\":[\"eyewitness identification no SCOTUS recent\",\"Manson reliability state high courts frontier\"]}\n{\"claim_id\":\"ABS-0105\",\"claim_text\":\"did not decide which post-attachment events require counsel\",\"subject\":\"Which post-attachment events require counsel (Rothgery reserved)\",\"search_terms_suggested\":[\"Rothgery post-attachment critical stage counsel\",\"which events require counsel not decided\"]}\n{\"claim_id\":\"ABS-0106\",\"claim_text\":\"the unsettled frontier of **pole cameras** (*[[United States v. Hay|Hay]]*), **ALPR**, and **drones** (bridged by *[[California v. Ciraolo|Ciraolo]]*/*[[Florida v. Riley|Riley]]*) — scale-dependent and split\",\"subject\":\"Unsettled digital-surveillance frontier (pole cameras, ALPR, drones)\",\"search_terms_suggested\":[\"pole camera ALPR drone frontier split\",\"digital surveillance scale-dependent unsettled\"]}\n{\"claim_id\":\"ABS-0107\",\"claim_text\":\"the unresolved **device forensic-search split**\",\"subject\":\"Device forensic-search circuit split at the border\",\"search_terms_suggested\":[\"border device forensic search split\",\"Cotterman Cano Touset device forensic split\"]}\n{\"claim_id\":\"ABS-0108\",\"claim_text\":\"whether that bar reaches Bivens claims brought in the same suit was left open\",\"subject\":\"Whether the FTCA judgment bar reaches Bivens claims in the same suit (Case Index)\",\"search_terms_suggested\":[\"FTCA judgment bar Bivens same suit\",\"Brownback King judgment bar Bivens\"]}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
